Rationale: The claim states that the 2004 World Series of Poker gold bracelet holder held the Commissioner position in the 2011 competition where Michael McDonald was the youngest person to win an event. Evidence shows Annie Duke was the 2004 gold bracelet holder and the 2011 Commissioner. However, evidence contradicts the claim that Michael McDonald was the youngest person to win an event in 2011. The evidence explicitly states he did not hold this distinction.
